:"https://api.github.com/users/bonsairobo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bonsairobo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bonsairobo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bonsairobo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bonsairobo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bonsairobo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bonsairobo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bonsairobo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bonsairobo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2022-12-17T06:45:54Z","updated_at":"2022-12-17T06:45:54Z","body":"From looking at the `AsBindGroup` derive macro implementation, the fallback image's `TextureView` is used when the binding's `Option<Handle<Image>>` is `None`. Because this relies on already having a view that matches the desired binding dimensions, I think the solution will require creating a separate `GpuImage` for each possible `TextureViewDimension`.\r\n\r\nQuoting the docs on `FallbackImage`:\r\n\r\n> `FallbackImage` defaults to a 1x1 fully white texture, making blending colors with it a no-op.\r\n\r\nAssuming this holds for any `TextureViewDimension`, it should be OK to create more fallbacks.\r\n\r\nThis solution would require removing the `Deref` impl from `FallbackImage`.\r\n\r\nI can take a swing at implementing this solution unless someone quickly yells at me that I should do something else ;)","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bevyengine/bevy/issues/comments/1356076577/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"bonsairobo","id":3229981,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyMjk5ODE=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubuserconte